{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Comparative-baseline trial catalogue: T-01 Context cap and decomposition tests a required basis exceeding one actor's cap, tighter caps and a coupled cannot-fit case; its first fixture ran twice and was reviewed, and successor CASE-2 ran twice but was not assessed. T-02 Intent to usable result tests a small feature from sufficient but ambiguous intent, not run. T-03 Composition conservation tests two valid bounded results under one outer contract, and T-04 Failure and missing assessment tests an observed failure alongside an unassessed required obligation; their shared T-03-04 fixture ran twice, not assessed. T-05 Compaction and actor change tests pause, cleared context and resumption by another actor; fixture ran twice, not assessed. T-06 Changed governing requirement, T-07 Defective acceptance oracle and T-08 Broader process use respectively test a requirement revision after partial construction, structurally passing but behaviourally defective output, and sourced decision analysis with uncertainty and stale evidence; none was run.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":74,
          "quote":"| T-08 Broader process use | a sourced decision analysis with uncertainty and stale evidence | facts, assumptions, judgments and authority stay distinct; the result is independently assessable | not run |",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F2.%20Trials%20from%20the%20comparative%20baseline",
          "start_line":74
        }
      ],
      "key":"comparative_trials",
      "label":"Trials from the comparative baseline"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "R-01 Fresh-context activation compares bounded activation on a declared subject by a fresh actor given only this corpus with the same task against the rc.2 corpus. Its fixture's five variants each ran twice, not assessed. R-02 No private knowledge repeats the task withholding validator folklore, author memory and whole-corpus loading; R-01 variant V1 ran twice, not assessed.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":89,
          "quote":"| R-02 No private knowledge | the same with validator folklore, author memory and whole-corpus loading withheld | the activation still succeeds or returns out_of_frame truthfully | fixture [R-01](../qualification/cases/R-01/CASE.md) variant V1 run twice; not assessed |",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F3.%20Recoverability",
          "start_line":89
        }
      ],
      "key":"recoverability_cases",
      "label":"Recoverability cases"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "CD cases exercise work-time distinctions through fresh constructors using the corpus on declared subjects with assessed results. CD-01 concerns peer actors without a central coordinator or familiar role names, an uncertain-effect handover and an independently scoped installed executive configuration; mechanisms are ACTIVATION §1 Configuration, §3 Effects, §5 and EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §16. CD-02 compares software and mixed human/software realisations and a faster plan sacrificing independent assessments and a human decision; mechanisms are SPEC_METHOD §11 rules 1, 2, 4 and EVALUATION §3. CD-03 resumes from a stale summary conflicting with the workspace and an effect record, with one resolution outside the actor's grant; mechanisms are ACTIVATION §5, §3 Effects and Construction availability, §7. All three are not run.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":101,
          "quote":"Each needs actual use, a fresh constructor applying this\ncorpus to a declared subject with the result assessed, in addition to the\nlogical review of §5.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F4.%20Cases%20from%20the%20common%20discriminators",
          "start_line":97
        }
      ],
      "key":"common_discriminator_cases",
      "label":"Common-discriminator actual-use cases"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Assurance-relation cases demonstrate applicable positive, negative and unresolved cases under FOUNDATIONS §4. AR-01 places in each actual-use expectation set a necessary condition that a wrong decision can satisfy. AR-02 records, per set, two admissible returns with identical observations but different correctness. AR-03 uses an expectation writer, actors and grader of one model family, with writer and actors reading the same owning sections. These first three are not run and await product-owner selection of criterion 4's actual-use trial. AR-04 changes two owning sections and adds nine against dependent curated frames, hashed expectations, interpretation and conservation readings; it was performed once by the author, whose retention claims await nonauthor readback.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":121,
          "quote":"The first three are exercised by the actual-use trial of\ncriterion 4 and are not run until the product owner selects it; the fourth\nwas performed once by the candidate's author.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F4.%20Cases%20from%20the%20common%20discriminators",
          "start_line":119
        }
      ],
      "key":"assurance_relation_cases",
      "label":"Assurance-relation cases"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A reasoned reviewer constructs a discriminator situation against the text and determines whether it yields the expected distinction, a counterexample or a contradiction, without running anything. The result belongs to EVALUATION §4 and the reviewer must meet §3. Structural checking does not establish this review, and the review supplies no actual-use evidence.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":140,
          "quote":"A logical-review check is a reviewer's reasoned reading: the reviewer\nconstructs a discriminator's situation against the text and finds whether\nthe text yields the expected distinction, or finds a counterexample or a\ncontradiction, without running anything (P6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Coverage%20of%20the%20common%20discriminators",
          "start_line":132
        }
      ],
      "key":"logical_review",
      "label":"Logical-review check"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Catalogue of 52 situations, numbered by the external construction specification. Each has L-n unless a case is specified; all remain subject to universal logical review. 1 derivation/independence claim: FOUNDATIONS §1, §3 and EVALUATION §1, premises shown. 2 omitted inherited deciding rules: FOUNDATIONS §3 and all family tables. 3 unchanged rival consumer rules beneath a new introduction: FOUNDATIONS §3, §2 and shared owners ACTIVATION §1–7/EVALUATION §3, §5. 4 shorter text without fewer entry reconciliations: FOUNDATIONS §3, README and those owners. 5 unification retaining a domain exception: FOUNDATIONS §4 Results refinements, §2 imports and refining members. 6 ODD reduced to vocabulary: ACTIVATION §1, §4, §5; ODD §1. 7 shared successor implementing several predecessor clauses and 8 deleted exception: RELEASE §9 and source dispositions. 9 shared-law replacement: FOUNDATIONS §2 and referring members. 10 generic rule owned only by optional profile: FOUNDATIONS §3, PROFILES §1, IDENTITY §2, ACTIVATION §1. 11 helper promoted to public mechanism: DESIGN_MODULE §4, ACTIVATION §6. 12 small interface asserted Markov: IDENTITY §2, WORLD_MODEL §4, FOUNDATIONS §5. 13 schema-valid a_c omission and 14 faithful fragment offered as whole interpretation: AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §6, AC-017/018 for 13, EVALUATION §2. 15 projection instead of quotation: AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §9, ACTIVATION §2. 16 unresolved premise treated as freedom: AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §9/AC-009, ACTIVATION §1. 17 several solutions: §9/AC-008. 18 not-required converted to prohibited or preference to obligation: EVALUATION §7, AC-008/§9. 19 stale interpretation marked current at entry: PRODUCT_DEFINITION §11, ACTIVATION §2, README. 20 representation versus information: EVALUATION §2/§6, AC-017/018, structure is not meaning. 21 unchanged identity with changed content: FOUNDATIONS §2, IDENTITY §2, RF-005, ACTIVATION §7. 22 incompatible typed producers/consumers: FOUNDATIONS §4, AC-004/016, T-03 plus L-22 for incompatible domain/precondition and same-shape fields. 23 failed A and uncovered B: FOUNDATIONS §4 conjunction, T-04 plus L-23 for authenticating each planned judgement and uncovered B. 24 planned judgement from another subject: conjunction second input, EVALUATION §2, RF-005; plan membership authenticates nothing. 25 interdependent context exceeding one actor: ACTIVATION §2 step 3/§4, RF-014; T-01. 26 byte-fit obscuring a dependency: ACTIVATION §2 steps 2–3, EVALUATION §7, RF-003/004; fit is not attention and actual use belongs to frame qualification. 27 changed frame/task after trial or answer-supplying instructions: EVALUATION §7 Adequate attention/§3 Protocol. 28 author reviewing own work in fresh context: EVALUATION §3, ACTIVATION §1 Reconfiguration; fresh context and contribution readback do not establish independent acceptance. 29 omitted frontier items: ACTIVATION §1 Open work outside attention, RF-015; out of view stays open. 30 newly discovered obligations or destination changed to pass: ACTIVATION §1/§5. 31 directly authorised task fitting a sufficient frame: ACTIVATION §1 Allocation, Direct entry, Roles and delegation. 32 peer configuration without central Executive/familiar roles and 33 redistribution with uncertain effects: ACTIVATION §1, EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §16 for 32, ACTIVATION §3/§5 for 33; CD-01. 34 familiarity/persistence/self-organisation called optimal: ACTIVATION §1 Optimality; optimality is separate. 35 compact result hiding delivery blocker: ACTIVATION §1 Coordination/§7. 36 changed dependency or invalidating observation: ACTIVATION §7/§1, EVALUATION §2, REFERENCE_FRAME §10; T-06 plus L-36. 37 rules without context/authority: REFERENCE_FRAME §11, ACTIVATION §1 Distinct relations/§2; rule packet is not activation. 38 stale summary versus workspace: ACTIVATION §5/§3; CD-03. 39 partly written interrupted work: ACTIVATION §5, FOUNDATIONS §4 Not performed; T-05 plus L-39. 40 successful parse/map: EVALUATION §2/§7, AC-018/019; T-07 plus L-40 for practical evidence. 41 process/carrier change proposed as law: ACTIVATION §6, SPEC_METHOD §4, TICKETS §5; purpose required. 42 requirements across executor kinds and 43 faster plan weakening independence/human authority: SPEC_METHOD §11 rules 1/2/4, EVALUATION §3 for 43; CD-02. 44 same calculus across environments or different operations by one actor: SPEC_METHOD §11 rules 2/5. 45 structurally valid human-process model: SPEC_METHOD §11 rule 6, AC-018; model selects no executor. 46 rival loci deciding one question: FOUNDATIONS §2, PRODUCT_DEFINITION §11; one owner per question. 47 member-specific result values: FOUNDATIONS §4, ACTIVATION §3 and defining members; refinements map once. 48 lifecycle/classification deciding admission/compliance/closure: FOUNDATIONS §4, ACTIVATION §3, TICKETS §3, SPEC_METHOD §2. 49 conserved heading with changed obligation or superseded row naming only old section: RELEASE §9 and source dispositions; compare meaning, required/permitted decisions, modality, triggers, scope and exceptions. 50 result-returning frame: every such frame, RF-012/§11, ACTIVATION §2 Standalone scope; carry result algebra. 51 functor/categorical join claim: FOUNDATIONS §4 Formal fragment, EVALUATION §6, AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §5; demonstration required. 52 rewrite/refinement: ACTIVATION §4; steps licensed.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":156,
          "quote":"The table states each common discriminator, numbered in the order the\ngoverning specification lists them, with the member sections it\nexercises, and the cases or the logical-review check\nthat exercise it.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Coverage%20of%20the%20common%20discriminators",
          "start_line":142
        },
        {
          "end_line":211,
          "quote":"| 52 | A rewrite or refinement step is applied | ACTIVATION §4 Refinement | L-52 steps are licensed |",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Coverage%20of%20the%20common%20discriminators",
          "start_line":211
        }
      ],
      "key":"member_discriminator_catalogue",
      "label":"Common member discriminator catalogue"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Integrated checks J53–J55 concern respectively conflicting shared decisions despite local passes, a clear replacement without owner acceptance of changed meaning, and five satisfied member criteria with a sixth missing, stale or falsified. They are whole-candidate construction/closure checks, not member predicates.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":216,
          "quote":"The construction and integrated closure checks of the common conformance\ntable are not member predicates. The integrated working assessment reads\nthem over the whole candidate, and the cross-family acceptance review\nevaluates them before closure:",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Coverage%20of%20the%20common%20discriminators",
          "start_line":213
        }
      ],
      "key":"integrated_closure_checks",
      "label":"Integrated closure checks"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Assessed under criterion 5 within a member's declared responsibility."],
      "definition": "Nine universal-construction situations and their named mechanisms/checks: UC-1 internal passes with end-to-end failure, ACTIVATION §1 composition, FOUNDATIONS §4 preservation, EVALUATION §1, L-UC1; UC-2 lawful operations missing outcome constraints, ACTIVATION §1 A/Z and SPEC_METHOD §11, L-UC2; UC-3 bug possibly in implementation, requirements or observation, ACTIVATION §1 diagnosis/SPEC_METHOD §4 triage, L-UC3; UC-4 weakened requirement making implementation pass, ACTIVATION §1 destination/completion, SPEC_METHOD §4, FOUNDATIONS §4 corrections preserve counterexamples, L-UC4; UC-5 prediction accuracy diverging from outcome attainment, ACTIVATION §1 three accounts/diagnosis, L-UC5; UC-6 strategy chosen by name or cheaper plan losing assurance, ACTIVATION §1, FOUNDATIONS §4 quantified assurance, EXECUTIVE_BASELINE Steel-thread delivery, L-UC6; UC-7 invariant preservation without delivery, ACTIVATION §1 and FOUNDATIONS §3, L-UC7; UC-8 exhausted limit, newly exposed work or continuing maintenance, ACTIVATION §1 Stops/§6, L-UC8; UC-9 restart/disturbance contradicting cached success, ACTIVATION §5/§7, CD-03 not run and L-UC9. Twelve assurance situations: AS-1 local passes without precondition/final-outcome implication, FOUNDATIONS §4 preservation, L-AS1; AS-2 correct histogram keys but incorrect counts, necessary-condition checking, AR-01 not run/L-AS2; AS-3 identical observations of admissible states with opposite obligation truth, observation sufficiency, AR-02 not run/finite assurance oracle/L-AS3; AS-4 implementation-copied expectation citing requirement digest, parallel derivation, L-AS4; AS-5 sound satisfied or indeterminate conclusions on the same observations, universal soundness covering all admitted conclusions, L-AS5; AS-6 agreement through shared error, parallel derivation, AR-03 not run/L-AS6; AS-7 multiplied miss rates without conditional independence or injected-defect score called whole-product correctness probability, quantified assurance, finite oracle/L-AS7; AS-8 finite examples/schema validity called universal proof, formal representation and AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §9 condition 1, L-AS8; AS-9 changed requirement with silently retained answers/evidence, change impact/ACTIVATION §7, AR-04 author-performed once/L-AS9; AS-10 implementation/environment change selected only by requirement-test provenance, change impact, finite oracle/L-AS10; AS-11 supported isolation of local repair from unchanged obligation and evidence conditions, retention, L-AS11; AS-12 cheap incomplete selection or overhead exceeding saved execution, change-impact cost/quantified assurance, L-AS12. Unless otherwise specified, assurance mechanisms are FOUNDATIONS §4. Expected distinctions are external, not restated here.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":254,
          "quote":"The construction specification adds, beside the member discriminators\nabove, nine universal-construction discriminators and twelve assurance\ndiscriminators, with their expected distinctions in the same file and not\nrestated here, assessed under criterion 5 within a member's declared\nresponsibility.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Coverage%20of%20the%20common%20discriminators%2FUniversal-construction%20and%20assurance%20discriminators",
          "start_line":244
        },
        {
          "end_line":278,
          "quote":"| AS-12 | Selection is cheap but omits a material obligation, or selection overhead exceeds the saved execution | FOUNDATIONS §4 Change impact and evidence reuse (cost); FOUNDATIONS §4 Quantified assurance | L-AS12 |",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Coverage%20of%20the%20common%20discriminators%2FUniversal-construction%20and%20assurance%20discriminators",
          "start_line":278
        }
      ],
      "key":"universal_assurance_catalogue",
      "label":"Universal-construction and assurance discriminators"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A provenance record that decides nothing: eight comparative trials are conserved in §2; builder-history counterexamples are new from common inputs and reacquire primary sources when designed for execution. The 52 member, J53–J55 of seven integrated-closure, and 21 universal/assurance situations come from the construction specification identified in the absent header. Their mapping, logical checks and §4 cases are new. This member makes no predecessor claim.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":303,
          "quote":"This section records dispositions and decides nothing.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F6.%20Source%20dispositions",
          "start_line":293
        }
      ],
      "key":"conformance_source_dispositions",
      "label":"Conformance source dispositions"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Applies to boundaries for which the profile is adopted."],
      "definition": "Tier-3 optional realisation-design profile covering ontology-first derivation, proportional sequencing, decision completeness, frame conservation, constructability and foundation selection, entity/authority/admission/function completeness, Prime atoms and contraction, IACS, three-view/invariant/computational design, modules, realisation rules, review, adoption and runtime identity defaults. It imports FOUNDATIONS, ACTIVATION, EVALUATION, IDENTITY, SPEC_METHOD, ASSURANCE, TICKETS and RELEASE without redefining their objects. ODD and UX refine or bound it within their scopes. Its own terms include Ontology, Prime, IACS, Subordinate Payload, Promotion Test, Boundary Inflation, carrier, three-view asset, module, decision_complete(B) and co_evolution_admissible(B).",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":26,
          "quote":"Tier 3. An optional profile of realisation design: ontology-first",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE",
          "start_line":3
        },
        {
          "end_line":32,
          "quote":"This profile's own terms are Ontology (the engineering Ontology of one\ndesigned boundary, §5), Prime (§5, §6), the Irreducible Architectural\nCarrier Set (IACS, §6), Subordinate Payload, Promotion Test and Boundary\nInflation (§6), carrier, three-view design asset (§7), module (§9) and the\npredicates `decision_complete(B)` and `co_evolution_admissible(B)` (§5).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE",
          "start_line":28
        }
      ],
      "key":"design_profile",
      "label":"DESIGN_MODULE"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["A boundary is governed by this profile."],
      "definition": "Declared profile-to-tier-2 binding: ASSURANCE's carrier inventory maps to IACS; accepted ontology and design to accepted Ontology and target design; domain/sequence/state projections to the three-view design asset; decision-completeness/co-evolution conditions to the two §5 predicates. Tier-2 law retains its meaning and applies unchanged to these bound objects.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":42,
          "quote":"Direction: profile to tier 2; preserved meaning: the tier-2 law applies\nunchanged to the bound objects; narrowed scope: boundaries this profile\ngoverns; invalidation: a change of this profile's definition of any bound\nobject re-evaluates the binding (P1, P6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE",
          "start_line":39
        }
      ],
      "key":"assurance_design_binding",
      "label":"Profile-to-ASSURANCE binding"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Performed evaluations return the FOUNDATIONS §4 core result algebra directly or through the defined reconstruction-decision and cross-view-axiom refinements. Ontology and design verdicts are ACTIVATION §3 dispositions. Other closed vocabularies are author-declared, assessed design-record entries rather than results: function derivation, entity-lifecycle entries, discovery/admission-form exclusions, competing paths, IACS revisions, reference mappings, two-part algorithmic dispositions and module roles. A record's evaluation has its own core value. A not_applicable record entry denotes exclusion with no result for the excluded obligation; a not_applicable axiom verdict is a value of a predicate whose declared disjunction includes non-application.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":73,
          "quote":"a consumer that combines this profile's outcomes with other\nresults reads each result in the one core and never reads a record entry\nas a result (P5, P6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE",
          "start_line":71
        }
      ],
      "key":"design_results_and_records",
      "label":"Design results, dispositions and record entries"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Realisation discipline aimed at reducing ambiguity, entropy, avoidable debt, hidden authority/mutation and semantic drift; improving refactorability; and preserving reconstructable audit evidence. It favours low coupling, modular composition, immutable typed carriers, total or nearly total transforms and explicit effect boundaries, without language ideology. A module boundary is one possible finite inspectable intermediate unit for reasoning, implementation, evaluation, proof and refactoring. Scope includes module boundaries, schema/carrier families, entity/record design and interfaces across languages and runtimes.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":98,
          "quote":"The profile is therefore about realisation design and implementation\nshape.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FPurpose",
          "start_line":97
        }
      ],
      "key":"realisation_design",
      "label":"Realisation design and bounded implementation units"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Scoped to boundaries governed by the profile."],
      "definition": "The core realisation-shape rule is owned once by SPEC_METHOD §2. Its stated diagnostic is that a reader needing orchestration to learn system meaning indicates excessive imperative design and coupling; every profile rule refines it.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":151,
          "quote":"The core rule, with the test that a design is too imperative and too\ncoupled when a reader has to inspect orchestration to learn what the\nsystem means, is stated once in\n[SPEC_METHOD §2 Realisation shape](SPEC_METHOD.md#realisation-shape),\nscoped to boundaries this profile governs; every rule below refines it",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FCore%20rule",
          "start_line":146
        }
      ],
      "key":"realisation_core_rule",
      "label":"Imported realisation core rule"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["An actor designs, implements or reviews a boundary governed by the profile."],
      "definition": "Material family F17 software design presents premise-to-consequence arguments and separately attributes domain/policy choices. Imports: F1 frames/context and authority kinds; F2 transitions/steps/configuration; F3 results/combination; F4 work state/resumption/reuse; F6 claims/evidence/assessment/acceptance; F8 identity; F10 constitutional chain/outcome/build-tenant binding; F12 project-method binding; F13 work carriers; F18 graph-native construction. Claimed commitment standing is P0 recovered; P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 independent; P4b derived from P0/P2 with non-reacquirable step facts; P5 derived from P0/P6 with P0's open-world premise. Adopted instance premises, not foundational consequences: I1 decided Product outcomes/capabilities and named-boundary adoption; I2 meaning can reside in typed carriers/transforms or orchestration/helpers/open payload/shared state and in several places; I3 bounded actors generally lack earlier design reasoning during later local work; I4 mechanisms may be local or existing foundations and computation recurs. The new table accounts for the head, binding and §1–12; §13 only records dispositions; its Pillar column follows FOUNDATIONS §3.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":182,
          "quote":"Its instance premises hold where a project\nadopts this profile for a boundary; they are adopted with it and do not\nfollow from the foundations (P1, P6):",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":180
        },
        {
          "end_line":277,
          "quote":"no profile choice is presented as following from the foundations (P6, P2).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":277
        }
      ],
      "key":"software_design_family",
      "label":"F17 foundation-to-law argument"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
